# DBTITLE 1,Generate Data — Repeat this section for EACH table
# ============================================================================
# DOMAIN-FIRST GENERATION PATTERN
# (LLM populates one cell per table in dependency order)
# ============================================================================
#
# The LLM generating this notebook uses the DOMAIN-FIRST pattern:
#
#   1. Define DOMAIN_COLS dict with ALL categorical/analytical columns
#      and their domain-specific values + weights from synthetic_data_spec.yaml
#   2. Call generate_table() — builds complete DataGenerator in one pass
#   3. Call enforce_varchar_limits() as safety net
#   4. Call verify_before_write() to catch any issues
#   5. Write to Delta table
#
# There is NO base_generator(). Every column is handled explicitly:
#   - Domain columns → values from DOMAIN_COLS dict
#   - FK columns → replaced with sampled parent keys
#   - PK columns → unique sequential values
#   - Everything else → type-appropriate random data
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXAMPLE: Dimension table
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
